    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d834">

                <pb facs="0913" n="1747" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.85/358</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-25T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 25, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your March 21, 8 p.m. You may say to the Minister for Foreign Affairs that this
                    Government has the matter of the purchase and change of flag of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bahia Blanca</hi> under careful consideration and
                    desires to be informed as to the routes proposed for her to follow in Government
                    or any other service. You may intimate that you believe that this Government
                    would be inclined to recognize transfer provided that voyages are satisfactory
                    to this Government and provided Argentine Government will give proper assurance
                    that the vessel carries no crew, officers, or passengers of enemy
                    nationality.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
